  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 (0.520 acc) clearly outperforms pca_n2000 (0.485 acc) in singleprofile RNA-only settings, and image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208), indicating RNA is the dominant signal. Uncertainty: We have no data yet on whether multiprofile + aggregation improves over singleprofile, and whether the benefit (if any) depends on the RNA encoder. This experiment (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) directly compares against config_004 (scvi_n200, singleprofile) to isolate the effect of multiprofile with simple average-pool aggregation while holding the encoder fixed. Choosing avgpool over transformer first is the more conservative, interpretable step: if simple averaging does not help, it questions the value of multiprofile broadly; if it does, it motivates testing transformer aggregation next. This is the highest-information single experiment under budget because it extends the best-performing configuration along one new design axis without introducing confounds (no new encoder, no image modality, no fusion)."
}

